course: dictionary
lesson: 3407
title: Explore: travel, test and search
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Explore is a verb, a doing word. It can mean to travel around a place you do not know, to test or think about something carefully, or to search with your hands or eyes. Context tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «Toddlers explore with their hands and mouths.» Here explore does not mean going on a trip. Hands and mouths are the clues: little children learn about things by touching and tasting them.
explain: «Step by step Portuguese ships crept down the coast of Africa, like a child exploring a dark corridor one door at a time.» Here explore means to go into unknown places carefully. Test your meaning: does «going into the unknown, one step at a time» fit? It does.
fact: Explore means to travel around a place you do not know, to find out what it is like.
fact: Explore can also mean to look at, test or think about something carefully to learn more about it.
fact: Explore can mean to search with your hands or eyes.
fact: The verb forms are explore, explores, explored and exploring. «Explored» shows something has already happened.
fact: «Explore» in maths means trying different numbers to find patterns, and in history explorers sailed to unknown lands.
exercise: «Toddlers explore with their hands and mouths.» What does explore mean here? | *To find out about things by touching and tasting | To sleep quietly in a warm bed | To run a long way from home
exercise: In science, children explore magnets by trying and watching. What does explore mean here? | To hide from a teacher | *To test something carefully to learn more about it | To buy something new | To travel to a faraway country
exercise: Which word fits? «The sailors ___ the coast of Africa last year.» | exploring | *explored | explore | explores
test: «Sam explores the old forest with his dad.» What does explore mean here? | To fall asleep under a tree | To cook a meal for the family | To shout loudly across the field | *To travel around a place to find out what it is like
test: Safety first: where should you explore an old mine? | Running in with friends after dark | *With an adult, never alone | Alone at night | Without telling anyone at home
exam: Which sentence uses explore to mean think about an idea carefully? | Ben wants to explore the cave after dark | Ben wants to explore the old mine alone | *Ben wants to explore the idea of a school garden | Ben wants to explore the sea in a small boat
